    explain: "Lessons 7 and 24 gave you あげます, もらいます and くれます; this lesson adds three more that adjust the verb to the standing of the two people involved. やります replaces あげます when the receiver is below you — a child, a subordinate, an animal or a plant — though with people modern Japanese often prefers あげます anyway. いただきます replaces もらいます when you receive something from someone above you, and くださいます replaces くれます when someone above you gives something to you. As with くれます, くださいます also covers gifts to a member of your own family.",
